    "description": "Game day just got even better thanks to this easy recipe for Stadium Nacho Cheese Sauce. In this video, Annie shows you how to make homemade nacho cheese sauce that’s tastier and cheesier than the kind you get at the stadium. To make this velvety smooth cheese sauce, start by melting some butter on the stovetop. Whisk in flour and milk until thickened, then stir in some processed cheese and a pinch of salt until melted. Pour over tortilla chips, then top with some pickled jalapeños for a classic stadium snack that you can enjoy from your very own couch. The best part? For these homemade nachos, you don’t even have to wait in line!",
